My rice for the simple terminal - st
--------------------
st is a simple terminal emulator for X which sucks less.


Requirements
------------
In order to build st you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install st (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running st
----------
If you did not install st with make clean install, you must compile
the st terminfo entry with the following command:

    tic -sx st.info

See the man page for additional details.

Keybinds
--------

MODKEY - Alt 
TERMMOD - Ctrl + Shift 

### Clipboard

| Keybind                | Action                                  |
|------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
| `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `C` | Copy selection to clipboard             |
| `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `V` | Paste from clipboard                    |
| `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `Y` | Paste primary selection                 |
| `Shift` + `Insert`     | Paste primary selection                 |

### Zoom

| Keybind                    | Action                  |
|----------------------------|-------------------------|
| `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `+`     | Zoom in (+2)            |
| `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `_`     | Zoom out (-2)           |
| `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `Home`  | Reset zoom              |

> `Ctrl+Shift+PageUp` / `Ctrl+Shift+PageDown` zoom bindings exist in the config but are commented out (disabled).

### Scrolling

| Keybind                | Action                  |
|------------------------|-------------------------|
| `Shift` + `Page Up`    | Scroll up               |
| `Shift` + `Page Down`  | Scroll down             |

### Printing / Misc

| Keybind                    | Action                          |
|----------------------------|---------------------------------|
| `Break`                    | Send break                      |
| `Ctrl` + `Print`           | Toggle printer                  |
| `Shift` + `Print`          | Print screen                    |
| `Print`                    | Print selection                 |
| `Ctrl` + `Shift` + `NumLock` | Toggle application keypad (numlock) |

## Mouse Shortcuts

| Mouse                  | Action                                              |
|------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
| Scroll wheel up        | Scroll up 1 line                                    |
| Scroll wheel down      | Scroll down 1 line                                  |
| Middle click (release) | Paste primary selection                             |
| `Shift` + wheel up     | Send `Page Up` (`\033[5;2~`) to the program         |
| `Shift` + wheel down   | Send `Page Down` (`\033[6;2~`) to the program       |
| Wheel up (alt screen)  | Send `Ctrl+Y` (`\031`) to the program               |
| Wheel down (alt screen)| Send `Ctrl+E` (`\005`) to the program               |

> When a program has mouse reporting enabled, hold `Shift` (`forcemousemod`) to force terminal selection and shortcuts.

## Selection

| Action                          | Result                      |
|---------------------------------|-----------------------------|
| Left click + drag               | Normal selection            |
| `Alt` + left click + drag       | Rectangular selection       |
| Double click (within 300 ms)    | Select word                 |
| Triple click (within 600 ms)    | Select line                 |

Words are delimited by a space only (`worddelimiters`).

## Special Key Sequences

Standard terminal key mappings are provided for compatibility with the Linux world.

### Modifier Encoding

For arrow keys and similar keys, the modifier is encoded in the escape sequence:

| Modifier                  | Code |
|---------------------------|------|
| `Shift`                   | 2    |
| `Alt`                     | 3    |
| `Shift` + `Alt`           | 4    |
| `Ctrl`                    | 5    |
| `Shift` + `Ctrl`          | 6    |
| `Ctrl` + `Alt`            | 7    |
| `Shift` + `Ctrl` + `Alt`  | 8    |

Example: `Ctrl` + `Up` sends `\033[1;5A`.

### Navigation Keys

| Key                       | Notes                                          |
|---------------------------|------------------------------------------------|
| Arrow keys                | Support all modifier combos above; application |
|                           | cursor mode aware                              |
| `Home` / `End`            | Mode-dependent sequences; `Shift+Home` clears  |
|                           | screen in normal mode                          |
| `Page Up` / `Page Down`   | `Ctrl` and `Shift` variants supported          |
| `Insert` / `Delete`       | `Shift` and `Ctrl` variants supported          |
| `Shift` + `Tab`           | Sends `\033[Z` (back-tab)                      |
| `Alt` + `Enter`           | Sends `ESC` + `CR`                             |
| `Enter`                   | Sends `CR`                                     |
| `Backspace`               | Sends `DEL` (`\177`)                           |
| `Alt` + `Backspace`       | Sends `ESC` + `DEL`                            |

### Function Keys

| Key           | Modifier support                                           |
|---------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| `F1`-`F12`    | Plain, `Shift` (F13-F24), `Ctrl` (F25-F36),                |
|               | `Super` (F37-F48), `Alt` (F49-F60)                         |
| `F13`-`F35`   | Mapped directly to the equivalent Shift/Ctrl sequences     |

`F1`-`F4` use `\033OP`..`\033OS`; `F5`-`F12` use `\033[15~`..`\033[24~`.

### Keypad

Numeric keypad keys (`KP_0`-`KP_9`, `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `.`, `Enter`) send 
application-mode sequences (`\033Op`...) when keypad application mode is 
enabled, and regular characters otherwise. Use `Ctrl+Shift+NumLock` to toggle.

## Related Settings

| Setting           | Value                                              |
|-------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| Font              | JetBrainsMono Nerd Font, 16px                      |
| Shell             | `/bin/sh`                                          |
| Terminal name     | `st-256color`                                      |
| Opacity           | 0.8 focused / 0.6 unfocused                        |
| Tab spaces        | 8                                                  |
| Cursor shape      | Block                                              |
| Default size      | 80 x 24                                            |

